"Souls from Earth sometimes drift into this world; most are reborn as beasts, and few keep memory."
"Under the Wrenwood shrine two mana currents cross, and the shrine was raised on that crossing."
"The shrine's worn figure is the Wayfarer, a small Divine of roads, long forgotten by the town."
"The Wayfarer's glimmercore lay dormant under the shrine's floor for some three hundred years."
"Alan's soul came loose as he dozed and drifted, and the crossing under the shrine caught it."
"No body waited for his soul, so the Wayfarer's core spent itself to weave one from the currents."
"The core wove a human, as the soul had been, in the Wayfarer's likeness: a small red-haired woman."
"The core dissolved into her as it wove, and what was left of it is the Mana Weaver trait."
"She speaks and reads the common tongue from the core, which heard three centuries of travelers."
"The currents lean to her because they take her for part of the crossing that made her."
"Mana Weaver shows her mana currents, auras and corruption, and lends her workings their mana."
"She finds what Mana Weaver does by reaching for the currents with intent; nothing tells her first."
"Her first shaping of raw current into force earns the skill Current Lash from the System."
"The System reads her as Human, Level 1, with one trait; an Appraisal shows Mana Weaver as ???."
"No mage alive holds Mana Weaver; only the oldest Divine records name anything like it."
"Renir, the Pillar of Lost Magic, would know the trait for what it is on sight."
"The shrine is empty now: its core is spent, and the carved figure is only stone."
